A='Alpöge (A_D: GRH for rational Dirichlet L-functions); no additional conjecture'
M='Masullo (conditional M: GRH for Hecke L-functions over every number field)'
work='GRH_NIGHT.tex, complexity section; '
add('CX-ALG-001','Every odd composite N has a Miller–Rabin witness a ≤ 2(log N)^2. Testing every such base gives deterministic polynomial-time primality testing. Geometric form: powering and square-root relations in G_m over Z/NZ.',A,'classical with an exact locator; the analytic hypothesis is discharged under the task’s A_D convention','Bach (1990), Theorem 2 p.372 and application p.373; Schoof (2008), Theorem 2.2, pp.105–106 (quadratic Dirichlet characters suffice)',work+'inherited CX_GRH CX-N01; ALPOGE_GCT C-GRH-02; BRIDGES Q08; archive companion cote28 scan3 via CX_GRH')
add('CX-ALG-002','PRIMES was already in deterministic P without either GRH input. Geometric form: the AKS test uses explicit finite cyclotomic algebras over Z/NZ.','neither; unconditional AKS theorem','classical with an exact locator; attribution correction','Agrawal–Kayal–Saxena, PRIMES is in P (2004), Theorem 4.1 and Theorem 5.1, together with 2019 erratum',work+'inherited ALPOGE_GCT C-GRH-02 and CX_GRH CX-N01 qualification')
add('CX-ALG-003','Units represented by integers below 3(log N)^2 generate (Z/NZ)^×. Equivalently every proper subgroup omits such a unit. This is a small generating-set statement for the finite group scheme of units, not a presentation of it.',A,'classical with an exact locator; original source locator carried from preceding run','Bach (1990), Section 6 Theorem 3 p.372; ALPOGE_GCT C-GRH-02',work+'ALPOGE_GCT Q-C-MILLER-BACH; G_m dictionary SGA3 VIII 1.1–1.2')
add('CX-ALG-004','For supplied prime p and prime r | p−1, one can find an r-th nonresidue in F_p deterministically in time polynomial in log p, without factoring the rest of p−1. It is an explicit nontrivial class of the Kummer quotient F_p^×/(F_p^×)^r.',A,'classical with an exact locator; inherited transfer','Bach (1990), Theorem 3 p.372 applied to the r-th-power subgroup; Shoup (1992), Proposition 9 p.10; CX_GRH CX-N02',work+'CX_GRH CX-N02; SGA4 IX 3.2 Kummer companion')
add('CX-ALG-005','Square roots of any a in F_p, for a supplied odd prime p, can be found or ruled out deterministically in polynomial time; quadratic polynomials can therefore be factored. Geometric form: compute points of the degree-two Kummer cover y²=a.',A,'classical with an exact locator; short transfer proof in CX-ALG-005','Menezes–van Oorschot–Vanstone, Handbook of Applied Cryptography, Algorithm 3.34 and Fact 3.35 p.100; replace its random step by CX-ALG-004',work+'newly written transfer; complements CX_GRH CX-N01–N02')
add('CX-ALG-006','Given p and the complete factorization p−1=∏r_i^{e_i}, a certified primitive root of F_p can be constructed deterministically in polynomial time under A_D. Geometric form: build a generator of G_m(F_p) from its primary components.',A+'; supplied complete factorization of p−1','inherited proved transfer with exact work locator; factorization input retained','CX_GRH CX-N03, as checked in OURS_INTAKE_CX_GRH_20261121.md §1; Bach Theorem 3 for each nonresidue',work+'CX_GRH CX-N03; ALPOGE_GCT C-GRH-02')
add('CX-ALG-007','A primitive root modulo p occurs among O((log p)^6) initial positive integers. This supplies a polynomial-size guaranteed candidate list; a list alone does not certify which entry generates G_m(F_p).',A,'classical with an exact locator','Shoup, Searching for Primitive Roots in Finite Fields (1992), author version Theorem 3 p.4 and Section 6 p.13',work+'CX_GRH CX-N04; distinction from CX-ALG-006')
add('CX-ALG-008','In a supplied finite field F_{p^m}, a specified prime r | p−1 has an r-th nonresidue constructible deterministically in poly(m log p). For r=2 and even m there is an unconditional construction. The field representation is supplied; this computes a Kummer-torsor class.',A+'; supplied irreducible polynomial defining F_{p^m}; characteristic-two quadratic case excluded','inherited theorem, now independently re-proved here; auxiliary source formula corrected in CX-ALG-016–018','CX_GRH CX-N13, original check in OURS_INTAKE_CX_GRH_20261121.md §1; fresh full proof in GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-ALG-017–018',work+'CX_GRH CX-N13 retains priority; finite-field realization, SGA1 V §7 and SGA4 IX3.2')
add('CX-ALG-009','Degree-d polynomials over a supplied finite field F_q can be factored deterministically in (d^{log d} log q)^{O(1)}. Geometric form: compute connected components and primitive idempotents of a finite étale algebra after square-free reduction.',M+'; the sufficient smaller family is RH for ζ_Q and ζ_{Q(ζ_{2ν},p^{1/ν})} for the ν≤d² used in the cited construction','conditional on M; inherited complete composition, not re-proved here','CX_GRH CX-N15; Adleman–Lenstra (1986), Theorem 1 p.350 and Algorithm A pp.350–351; BGL (2001), Theorem 2 p.7; IKRS (2008), Main Theorem p.3, Lemma 4.2 p.14 and Proposition 4.6 pp.16–17',work+'CX_GRH CX-N15; current A_D-only gate CX_GRH CX-U02')
add('CX-ALG-010','The general deterministic factoring bound remains quasipolynomial. Its A_D-only extension reduces to constructing a prime-degree F_{p^r}, equivalently a maximal Teichmüller coefficient unit, in the residual higher-valuation cases.','Alpöge alone; additional prime-degree field construction remains missing in the displayed cases','open, with a strictly smaller gate proved in CX-ALG-023–025: p>d, r∤p(p−1)m, v_r(p^{ord_r(p)}−1)>1 for supplied F_{p^m}; only actually encountered r are needed','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-ALG-023–025; inherited CX_GRH CX-U02/CX-N14–N15 and intake §1/§5',work+'strict refinement of CX_GRH CX-U02; old degree-sr and extra BGL construction replaced by prime-degree witness')
add('CX-ALG-011','Ideal classes of a number field K are generated by prime ideals of norm at most 12(log |D_K|)^2. In geometry this is a bounded divisor generating set for Pic(Spec O_K).',M+'; class-character Hecke factors over K suffice, or RH for ζ of its Hilbert class field together with the stated factors','conditional on M; classical with exact locator; no relation-search bound added','Bach (1990), Theorem 4 p.375 and corollary p.376; original locator carried; fresh author-paper corroboration delegated to number_theory',work+'CX_GRH CX-N07; ALPOGE_BRIDGES CC-F03/F03b; SGA4 IX Theorem 3.3; cote2 scan5 via CX_GRH')
add('CX-ALG-012','A small class-group factor base does not itself give a polynomial-time algorithm for its full relation lattice or regulator. The missing work is relation collection, saturation and quantitative verification. Geometric form: generators of Pic do not present principal-divisor relations.',M+'; additional relation/height algorithms needed','open, with its gate: a polynomial bound for the appropriate relation search and saturation; no implication of impossibility claimed','CX_GRH CX-N07–N08, CX-U03; RETURN_CX_GRH_final_IMPLICATIONS.md §1',work+'class-group computation gate retained')
add('CX-ALG-013','The usual GRH class-group conclusions over an abelian field K/Q are not automatically A_D-only: the Hilbert class field may be nonabelian over Q. A_D suffices if that larger field is abelian.','Alpöge for abelian Hilbert class fields; Masullo conditional in general','inherited exact hypothesis classification','CX_GRH CX-N07 and OURS_INTAKE_CX_GRH_20261121.md §1; Artin formalism for the Hilbert class field',work+'CX_GRH CX-N07; arithmetic Picard/Galois-cover companion')
add('CX-ALG-014','General integer factorization is not supplied by the cited primality or finite-field polynomial-factorization algorithms. The elementary proposed extraction from a Miller witness by gcd(a,N), gcd(a^m−1,N), gcd(a^m+1,N) already fails for N=35,a=2,m=17.','neither for the counterexample; an additional integer-factor extraction algorithm for the general task','proved here: the specified extraction is refuted; general deterministic polynomial-time factoring remains an open gate in this catalogue','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-ALG-014, direct modular computation',work+'new diagnostic; separates G_m over a known field from Z/NZ with unknown factorization')
add('CX-HN-001','Feasibility of rational/integer arithmetic-circuit polynomial systems over C belongs to AM⊆Π₂^P conditional on M; homogeneous nonzero feasibility is included. Geometric form: nonemptiness of a circuit-presented affine scheme, or of its projectivization.',M+'; Koiran arithmetic height/degree bounds and AM protocol','conditional on M; classical with exact locator','Koiran, DIMACS 96-27, Section 2 Theorem 2 pp.5–6; Section 5 Theorem 9 and Corollary 1 printed p.12 (PDF13); 8 August 1997 erratum p.1; GCT V Theorem 2.10 p.25',work+'CX_GRH CX-K01–K02; BRIDGES Q07')
add('CX-HN-002','The analytic input in Koiran is RH for ζ_E of one bounded algebraic solution field E; it need not be Galois. The finite étale cover Spec O_E[1/B] detects degree-one reductions.','Masullo conditional supplies this; no Artin holomorphy input required','classical exact input localization, already identified in preceding run','Koiran, DIMACS Section 5 Theorem 9 and Corollary 1 printed p.12 (PDF13); CX_GRH CX-K01; LO77 Theorem 1.1 for E/E',work+'CX_GRH CX-K01; SGA1 V §7; cote98 scans11–12 via CX_GRH')
add('CX-HN-003','The bounded abelian-witness promise version of HN is in AM under A_D: satisfiable instances must admit an abelian solution field with the explicit single-exponential degree, log-discriminant and denominator bounds used by Koiran.','Alpöge; bounded abelian-witness promise, including all stated arithmetic size bounds','inherited proved promise transfer','CX_GRH CX-K03; OURS_INTAKE_CX_GRH_20261121.md §1 and §4.1',work+'CX_GRH CX-K03; BRIDGES Q07 restricted form')
add('CX-HN-004','The proposed universal replacement by an abelian solution field is false: x³−2 has no root in any abelian extension of Q. Geometric form: this connected cubic finite étale generic fiber cannot be dominated by an abelian Q-cover containing its point.','neither; elementary Galois theory','inherited refutation with counterexample; not a logical independence claim','CX_GRH CX-K04; ALPOGE_GCT C-GRH-03; OURS_INTAKE_CX_GRH_20261121.md §1',work+'BRIDGES Q07 abelian-route obstruction')
add('CX-GEO-001','Conditional on M, feasibility of an existential Boolean combination of polynomial equalities and inequations given by rational arithmetic circuits is in AM. Its emptiness is in coAM⊆Σ₂^P. Geometric form: nonemptiness of an explicitly presented constructible locus.',M+'; circuit encoding has explicit variables and polynomial-length rational constants','proved here, conditional on M','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-GEO-001: Boolean selector and inverse-variable reduction to CX-HN-001',work+'new consequence; EGA constructible-locus language; complements CX_GRH CX-K02')
add('CX-GEO-002','For circuit-given f_1,…,f_s,g over Q, deciding g∈√(f_1,…,f_s) is in coAM under M, and nonmembership is in AM. The complementary witness system is f_i=0, yg−1=0. Geometric form: the principal open D(g) in V(f) is empty.',M+'; Hilbert Nullstellensatz and rational-to-complex faithful base change','proved here, conditional on M','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-GEO-002, full Rabinowitsch reduction proof',work+'new equation-access consequence for potential GCT separators; CX_GRH CX-K02')
add('CX-GEO-003','Inclusion and equality of affine algebraic sets specified by rational circuit equations are in coAM under M. For X=V(f),Y=V(g), X⊄Y iff f_i(x)=0 and ∑u_jg_j(x)=1 is feasible. Scheme-theoretic ideal inclusion is a separate task.',M+'; supplied defining equations; reduced underlying sets are the objects compared','proved here, conditional on M','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-GEO-003; empty-list and equality cases treated in full',work+'new practical containment gate; GCT orbit closures only when their defining equations are supplied')
add('CX-GEO-004','Let E_1,E_2 be subfields of a finite Galois L/Q. If their permutation characters differ, their numbers of degree-one primes differ at some unramified p≤(4 log|D_L|+2.5[L:Q]+5)^2. Prescribed primes S can be excluded by replacing L with L(√∏_{p∈S}p). Geometric form: finite Frobenius trace testing for finite étale covers.','Masullo conditional; Alpöge suffices if L/Q is abelian; the precise analytic input is RH for ζ_L (or enlarged ζ_L′) and ζ_Q','proved here, conditional on the stated input; explicit classical constant freshly located','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-GEO-004; Bach–Sorenson (1996), Theorem 5.1 p.1729, assumptions Section 2 p.1720',work+'new finite-level diagnostic; SGA1 V §7 and finite G-set companion cote98 scans11–12; connects AG recognition results')
add('CX-GEO-005','Equality of all Frobenius traces need not identify a finite étale cover up to isomorphism: GL_3(F_2) acts on its seven nonzero vectors and seven nonzero dual vectors with equal permutation character but nonisomorphic G-sets. Thus CX-GEO-004 certifies equality of rational permutation representations, not of G-sets.','neither; finite group linear algebra','proved here: explicit counterexample to the proposed trace-to-isomorphism inference','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-GEO-005, full character and stabilizer proof',work+'new diagnostic; Grothendieck Galois categories SGA1 V §7; finite G-set lambda-ring caveat')
add('CX-GEO-006','With an explicitly supplied polynomial/rational algebraic-group action, orbit membership is in AM conditional on M by encoding the action and invertibility. This does not replace orbit-closure membership when closure equations are unavailable.','Masullo conditional; polynomial-length circuit descriptions for group equations, action and inverted denominators','proved here, conditional on M','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-GEO-006; direct constructible-feasibility reduction to CX-GEO-001',work+'new GCT input/output refinement; SGA3 I group-action companion; cote28 scan3 via CX_GRH')
add('CX-NN-001','For a standard-graded algebra with explicitly listed variables and circuit-given homogeneous equations, a linear h.s.o.p. with polynomial output bits is constructible in FP^{Σ₂^P} conditional on M; polynomial space suffices unconditionally. Geometric form: construct a finite projection Spec R→A^{dim R}.',M+'; standard grading and equation access, explicit ambient variable list','inherited proved refinement; conditional on M','CX_GRH CX-K05; GCT V Theorem 3.4 pp.27–28, whose proof directly uses Σ₂ feasibility tests',work+'CX_GRH CX-K05; EGAII6.1.4–6.1.5 companion; cote98 scan44 via CX_GRH')
add('CX-NN-002','The historical EXPH construction/verification of strict small separating systems transfers conditional on M. It preserves the succinct output convention and all hypotheses. Geometric form: construct a finite separating projection with permitted polynomial slack in target dimension.',M+'; Mulmuley’s explicit-variety and output conventions','classical with exact locator, conditional on M; not the best bound for every construction task','GCT V Theorems 4.10 p.34 and 5.12; CX_GRH CX-K06',work+'CX_GRH CX-K06; equation/verification distinctions retained')
add('CX-NN-003','For the cited border-circuit setting, polynomial-space hitting-set constructions and resulting small normalization maps already hold unconditionally. Parameters n,s,r are in unary; polynomial space is not polynomial time.','neither; earlier unconditional results','classical with exact locator; credit correction','Forbes–Shpilka, ECCC TR17-163, Theorem 7.1 p.21 and Theorems 1.2–1.3 pp.3–4; Guo–Saxena–Sinhababu (2019), Theorems 1.5–1.6',work+'CX_GRH CX-K07; GCT V historical upper-bound replacement')
add('CX-NN-004','The optimal-cardinality h.s.o.p. bounds in the cited historical GCT V route for succinct explicit varieties retain their stated efficient defining-equation access; M does not itself compute those equations. This is a hypothesis of that route, not a universal necessity claim.','Masullo conditional plus singly exponential defining-equation computation where required','classical with exact locator; retained nonanalytic gate of the cited route','GCT V Theorems 4.1 p.30 and 5.5; CX_GRH CX-K06',work+'CX_GRH CX-K06; open uniform equation-access row')
add('CX-LIM-001','Neither stated zero-location input supplies a general polynomial-time PIT hitting set, a BPP=P theorem, or a GCT border-hardness lower bound in the cited routes. The exact remaining gate is the appropriate uniform hitting-set construction or the independent hardness hypothesis.','Alpöge/Masullo plus separate unproved algorithmic or circuit-hardness hypotheses would be needed by these routes','open, with its gate; this is route bookkeeping, not a proof of logical nonimplication','GCT V Theorem 2.4, Theorem 4.7 and Lemma 4.8 pp.32–33; CX_GRH CX-E06 (model distinction only)',work+'GCT_NSRH/GCT_PLETH/GCT_KRON gates; no P-vs-NP or VP-vs-VNP claim')
add('CX-LIM-002','Purity or nonnegative multiplicities do not by themselves supply efficient counting or occurrence obstructions. The supplied earlier runs already isolate positive finite-scheme #SAT encodings and PH1 counterexamples; actual quotient multiplicities and uniform construction remain required.','neither; independent geometric/computational counterexamples from previous runs','carried as background without fault found; no fresh whole-proof check of absent prior TeX','ALPOGE_GCT P-F7 and P-F10; PLETH PLE-F5/F7; RETURN_ALPOGE_GCT_cp01_IMPLICATIONS.md §§1–4',work+'open GCT uniform positivity and actual quotient-rank gates')
add('CX-LIM-003','The ETH/counting consequences in the CX_GRH return require its separate premise E. Tonight’s A_D and M do not include E, so those E-only rows are not activated in this catalogue.','neither of A_D/M alone; separate counting theorem E is required by those inherited proofs','proved scope classification, not a new ETH theorem','RETURN_CX_GRH_final_IMPLICATIONS.md premise contract and §3; OURS_INTAKE_CX_GRH_20261121.md §1 ETH table',work+'CX_GRH CX-E01–E05 excluded from A_D/M consequence transfer')
add('CX-GEO-007','With explicit ambient coordinates and polynomial action circuits, orbit-closure membership is in PSPACE unconditionally for GL_n actions extending to Mat_n and for SL_n actions. The SL_n reduction uses an explicit polynomial elementary-unipotent parameterization containing the big cell. Geometric form: membership in a polynomial-map image closure, without first computing defining equations.','neither; classical APS-in-PSPACE theorem plus the stated representation encoding','proved here as a short reduction to a classical theorem; no AM improvement asserted','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-GEO-007; Guo–Saxena–Sinhababu (2019), Theorem1.3 p5, Lemma4.1 and Theorem4.2 pp15–16',work+'new precise orbit-closure route; ambient encoding gate retained for succinct GCT inputs')
add('CX-GEO-008','Frobenius classes at unramified primes p≤(4log|D_L|+2.5[L:Q]+5)^2 detect every proper subgroup of G=Gal(L/Q); arbitrary representatives collectively generate G, and a sublist of ≤floor(log₂|G|) suffices. Prescribed bad primes are excluded using CX-GEO-004. Geometric form: a finite Frobenius certificate for a specified finite quotient of arithmetic π₁.','Masullo conditional; Alpöge suffices for abelian L/Q; precise zeta hypotheses as in CX-GEO-004','proved here, conditional on the stated zeta input','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-GEO-008; explicit Chebotarev plus a full double-counting derangement proof',work+'ORDER item30 effective Galois images; SGA1 V§7; cote98 scans11–12 via CX_GRH')
add('CX-ALG-015','Given N and a positive integer T divisible by λ′(N)=lcm_{p|N}(p−1), complete integer factorization is deterministic in poly(log N+log T) under A_D. Supplied φ(N) or λ(N) therefore suffice. Geometric form: an exponent annihilating the reduced residue multiplicative fibers permits small quadratic characters to separate unknown prime supports.',A+'; supplied exponent multiple T, with its full binary length charged','classical promise theorem with exact locator; input-length form proved here','Miller1976 Lemma5 and Theorem3 p310; GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-ALG-015 full input-length proof using Bach generator bound',work+'refines the integer-factor extraction gate CX-ALG-014; ORDER28; group-action companion cote28 scan3 carried from CX_GRH')
add('CX-ALG-016','The fixed-generator weighted resolvent in BIMS17 Theorem3.1 can vanish: over F7, f=X³−2 and ζ3=4 give α+4α^7+2α^49=0, contradicting the displayed nonresidue power formula. This refutes that literal formula, not the nonresidue-construction conclusion.','neither; exact finite-field arithmetic','proved here: explicit counterexample; corrected formulation CX-ALG-017','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-ALG-016; BIMS17 authorPDF Theorem3.1 p3 visually checked',work+'source audit for inherited CX_GRH CX-N13; Kummer eigenspace nonvanishing gate, SGA4 IX3.2')
add('CX-ALG-017','In a supplied extension E/Fq of degree d=rk with primitive ζr in Fq, odd r|(q−1), or r=2 and 4|(q−1), scanning a power basis finds a nonzero weighted Frobenius resolvent β with β^{(q^d−1)/r}=ζr^{-1}. It and its norm are r-th nonresidues, computable in poly(d log q).','neither given ζr; Alpöge supplies needed prime-field ζr in the inherited CX-N13 application','proved here as an explicit repair; the resulting A_D extension theorem is inherited, not claimed anew','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-ALG-017, complete projection/nonvanishing/exponent proof',work+'repairs literal BIMS17 Theorem3.1; independently re-proves odd-r branch of CX_GRH CX-N13; Kummer sequence SGA4 IX3.2')
add('CX-ALG-018','For odd p and even m, a quadratic nonresidue in a supplied F_{p^m} is constructible unconditionally in poly(m log p): direct trace-zero element when p≡1 mod4 or 4|m; otherwise norm-one square-root iteration in the F_{p²} subfield, followed by odd-degree inclusion.','neither; supplied irreducible polynomial and finite-field linear algebra','inherited theorem independently re-proved in full; no priority claim over BIMS17 Cor1.3 or CX_GRH CX-N13','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-ALG-018 full two-case proof; prior CX_GRH CX-N13; BIMS17 Cor1.3 authorPDF p2',work+'fresh complete proof preserves inherited unconditional case despite auxiliary source gap; SGA1 V§7 and SGA4 IX3.2')
add('CX-GEO-009','With unary pole/precision bound B and syntactic-degree bound D, existence of a Laurent-polynomial arc β with exponents in [−B,B] and F(β)−w in εC[ε]^m is in AM under M. Image-closure membership therefore has an AM promise version when positive instances admit polynomially bounded such arcs. Geometric form: finite Laurent jets of an explicit parameterized degeneration.',M+'; division-free rational action/map circuits, explicit variables, B and D charged in unary; A_D requires a bounded abelian witness for the coefficient system itself','proved here, conditional on M; the general polynomial-precision promise remains an additional gate','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-GEO-009 full coefficient-circuit reduction; Koiran HN theorem; GSS2019 Lemma4.1/Theorem4.2 pp15–16',work+'ORDER28 Koiran/GCT; refines CX-GEO-007 image-closure route; SGA3 I4.6.3.1 and4.7.1–2; cote28 scan3 via CX_GRH')
add('CX-ALG-019','For negative fundamental discriminant −d, the full imaginary-quadratic ideal class group is computable by a Las Vegas algorithm in expected exp((3/√8+o(1))√(log d loglog d)) time conditional on M. Detected failure is restarted; randomness and the subexponential, non-polynomial input-length bound are retained. Geometric form: compute Pic(Spec O_K) with its principal-divisor relations.',M+'; fundamental discriminant input; the cited class-character Hecke estimates and certified class-number comparison','inherited complete algorithmic transfer; primary theorem/input/algorithm statements freshly checked','CX_GRH CX-N12; Biasse–Erukulangara MainTheorem p4, Algorithm4 p15 and Corollary1 p16; JMV2009 Theorem1.1/Cor1.3',work+'CX_GRH CX-N12; SGA4 IXTheorem3.3, SGA6 V3.10 and VI3.2–3.3; cote2 scan5 via prior crosswalk')
add('CX-ALG-020','For fixed field degree n and B>2, degree-one primes of norm≤x with x≥(log Q)^B and their inverses give ray-class Cayley walks reaching any subset T with probability≥|T|/(2|G|) after C_{n,B} log|G|/loglog Q steps, for sufficiently large Q=|D_K|N(m). Precise adjacency estimates are λ1=2li(x)+O(n√x log(xQ)) and |λχ|=O(n√x log(xQ)); the latter constants are absolute.','Masullo conditional for the relevant finite-order narrow-ray-class Hecke characters; Alpöge suffices when K=Q','classical with exact locator; random walks remain randomized and n,B are fixed in the mixing conclusion','Jao–Miller–Venkatesan2009 Theorem1.1 authorp3, Remark1.2(a)/Cor1.3 p4, proofs pp7–10',work+'quantitative mixing input behind CX_GRH CX-N12/CX-ALG-019; arithmetic Picard correspondences SGA4 IXTheorem3.3; cote2 scan5')
add('CX-ALG-021','For imaginary quadratic K, the genus quotient Cl(O_K)/Cl(O_K)^2 satisfies the small-prime spectral/mixing conclusions CX-ALG-020 under A_D alone. Its Hecke characters factor as products of rational Dirichlet L-functions through the abelian genus field. If Cl(O_K) has exponent two this covers its entire graph. Prime ideals of prime norm≤(8log|D_K|+15)² generate this quotient under A_D, using a degree-four class field for each nontrivial character.','Alpöge; classical class field theory and JMV character-by-character estimates; no M input','proved here as a precise quotient-level input refinement','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-ALG-021 full generalized-dihedral/genus-field/character proof; JMV2009 Remark1.2(a) p4 and proof of Theorem1.1 p9; Bach–Sorenson Theorem5.1 p1729 for the explicit quotient generator bound',work+'sharpens CX-ALG-013 and inherited CX_GRH CX-N07–N12 hypothesis split; Picard quotient, SGA4 IXTheorem3.3; cote2 scan5')
add('CX-ALG-022','For ordinary elliptic curves over a fixed Fq with fixed point count and the same geometric endomorphism order, prime-degree isogenies below (log(4q))^B, B>2, form the cited expanding graph under M. A solver for discrete logarithms on a fraction μ of that level transfers to every curve on it with expected μ^{-1}poly(log q) overhead; no solver is supplied by this theorem.','Masullo conditional; imaginary-quadratic ring-class Hecke input, ordinary/same-level promise, and an independently supplied solver for the reduction conclusion','classical with exact locator, conditional on M; randomness retained','JMV2009 Theorem1.5 authorp5; Theorem1.6 pp6–7; Proposition3.1 p11, Theorem3.3 p12, proofs pp12–14',work+'ORDER20 elliptic/abelian-variety programme; CM ideal-class action and finite isogeny correspondences; cote2 scan5 Picard companion')
add('CX-ALG-023','For distinct primes p,r, an explicit F_{p^r} and a maximal equivariant Teichmüller unit in Fp[ζr] are polynomial-time interconstructible. The unit has exact order r^{v_r(p^{ord_r(p)}−1)}. A supplied F_{p^m} therefore supplies it unconditionally whenever r|m, even in the higher-valuation branch. Geometric form: a Kummer cover followed by finite étale descent.','neither; supplied prime-degree field or coefficient unit; supplied field degree m is charged to input size','classical equivalence with exact locator; new application to the prior finite-field gate proved here in full','Lenstra1991 Theorems5.1–5.2 pp338–340, Theorem3.1 pp334–336; GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-ALG-023 complete normal-basis/product-projection and invariant-field proof',work+'strictly extends CX_GRH CX-N14/CX-U02 cases; SGA1 V§7, SGA4 IX3.2; inherited group-action companion cote28 scan3')
add('CX-ALG-024','For odd prime r≠p, A_D makes RH for ζ_{Q(p^{1/r})} equivalent to RH for ζ_{Q(ζr,p^{1/r})}, via ζ_E=ζ_{Q(ζr)}(ζ_{Q(p^{1/r})}/ζ_Q)^{r−1}. It supplies q≡1 mod r with p^{(q−1)/r}≠1 mod q and q≤[4r(2r−3)log r+4(r−1)²log p+2.5r(r−1)+5]², hence an explicit F_{p^r} in poly(r log p).','Alpöge plus RH for one pure degree-r Dedekind zeta; Masullo supplies that extra input conditionally','proved here: exact permutation-character reduction and explicit discriminant/prime bound; field algorithm classical','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-ALG-024 full proof; Bach–Sorenson1996 Theorem5.1 p1729 and §2p1720; Adleman–Lenstra1986 AlgorithmA pp350–351, Lemma6 p352',work+'strict analytic-family refinement of CX_GRH CX-N11–N15; Artin finite-cover identity, SGA1 V§7; representation-ring companion SGA6 V§§2,7')
add('CX-ALG-025','Degree-d factoring over supplied F_{p^m} remains deterministic quasipolynomial under A_D plus RH only for pure fields Q(p^{1/r}), r≤d prime with r∤(p−1)m and v_r(p^{ord_r(p)}−1)>1. Only actually encountered such r are needed. If no such r exist it is A_D-only; p≤d is unconditional polynomial. If every prime r≤d divides m or has valuation one, the quasipolynomial bound is unconditional. Geometric form: primitive-idempotent computation in the Frobenius-fixed split finite étale algebra.','Alpöge plus the displayed finite pure-prime-degree zeta family; Masullo supplies it conditionally; no additional analytic input when the family is empty','proved here as a new complete composition and strictly smaller sufficient gate; bound (d^{log d} log(p^m))^{O(1)} retained','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-ALG-025 full proof; CX-ALG-023/024; IKRS published authorPDF Theorem5.8 pp28–29, Proposition4.6 pp18–19, Lemma4.2 p16',work+'moves CX_GRH CX-U02 and refines CX-N15 from ν≤d² Kummer fields to pure prime degrees≤d; ORDER28; SGA1 V§7 and SGA4 IX3.2')
add('CX-ALG-026','An explicit degree-n extension of supplied F_{p^m} is constructible in poly(n log(p^m)) from A_D and RH for pure Q(p^{1/r}) only at prime divisors r|n not covered by r=p, r|m, r|p−1 or valuation one. If every prime divisor r of n divides pm or has r≠p and valuation one, no analytic hypothesis is needed. In particular primes supported on pm suffice unconditionally. Geometric form: construct a connected degree-n finite étale cover.','Alpöge plus the displayed finite pure-prime-degree zeta family, conditionally supplied by Masullo; n unary or equivalent dense-output encoding','proved here as a complete input refinement of a classical field-construction theorem','GRH_NIGHT.tex CX-ALG-026 full transfer proof; Lenstra1991 Theorem9.1 pp344–346, Theorem7.1 p342 and Theorem1.1 p330; CX-ALG-023/024',work+'CX_GRH CX-N15/CX-U02 construction interface; ORDER28; SGA1 V§7')
(R/'rows.json').write_text(json.dumps(rows,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
